1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,166
UFO files.

2
00:00:02,331 --> 00:00:03,379
Real or not?

3
00:00:03,964 --> 00:00:06,587
The president says a UFO passed an F-22.

4
00:00:08,567 --> 00:00:13,566
On November 8, the president told a
national TV interview that Air Force

5
00:00:13,586 --> 00:00:18,028
pilots saw a round object pass an
F-22 at three times its speed.

6
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:20,658
He said it was not
aerodynamic, and that the

7
00:00:20,678 --> 00:00:23,232
pilots were credible, not
conspiracy theorists.

8
00:00:23,472 --> 00:00:26,386
But he also said he is not too much of a
believer.

9
00:00:26,626 --> 00:00:29,972
In October, he gave a different number:
four times the speed.

10
00:00:30,212 --> 00:00:34,807
He named no pilots, no date and no place,
and showed no radar or video.

11
00:00:36,167 --> 00:00:41,077
Since May, the Pentagon has been posting
its UFO files online, in batches.

12
00:00:41,317 --> 00:00:43,813
The program is called
Pursue, and it began after

13
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:45,962
the president ordered the
files released.

14
00:00:46,202 --> 00:00:51,034
The first batch had 162 files, and about
two thirds were partly blacked out.

15
00:00:51,274 --> 00:00:55,075
By October, there were seven batches, the
latest on October 23.

16
00:00:55,315 --> 00:00:59,199
By July, the site had drawn more than 1.7
billion visits.

17
00:01:00,567 --> 00:01:04,833
One file describes a sighting by FBI
agents in 2026.

18
00:01:05,073 --> 00:01:09,827
They saw a black triangle, 9 to 15 feet
wide, with no visible engines.

19
00:01:10,067 --> 00:01:13,670
It rose above a ridgeline,
hovered for about twenty seconds,

20
00:01:13,690 --> 00:01:17,233
then shot into a canyon in 2 to 3
seconds, without a sound.

21
00:01:17,473 --> 00:01:20,537
Their thermal camera showed the same heat
across its whole surface.

22
00:01:20,777 --> 00:01:23,154
The Pentagon report says
the witnesses estimated

23
00:01:23,174 --> 00:01:25,501
the speed, and the object
was never identified.

24
00:01:26,867 --> 00:01:30,949
Another file is an FBI interview with a
senior intelligence official.

25
00:01:31,189 --> 00:01:34,620
During an aerial search near a
military site, glowing objects

26
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:38,467
flared into view in groups of four
or five for about thirty minutes.

27
00:01:38,707 --> 00:01:42,223
One came within about ten feet of the
helicopter, then changed direction.

28
00:01:42,463 --> 00:01:45,299
Infrared showed them as super
hot, and they flew about

29
00:01:45,319 --> 00:01:48,154
twenty miles at speeds the
helicopter could not match.

30
00:01:48,394 --> 00:01:49,735
The file does not give the date.

31
00:01:49,975 --> 00:01:53,596
A former head of the Pentagon's UFO
office says he found nothing unexpected

32
00:01:53,616 --> 00:01:57,236
in it, and skeptics say infrared and
night vision can distort what you see.

33
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:00,687
The files also reach far back in time.

34
00:02:00,927 --> 00:02:05,582
In 1952, three Boy Scouts at a
camp in California said a silent

35
00:02:05,602 --> 00:02:09,737
silver object climbed, turned,
and seemed to fall apart.

36
00:02:09,977 --> 00:02:15,420
In 1957, a B-52 crew tracked an unknown
target near Saudi Arabia for up to seven

37
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:20,745
minutes, and investigators said the
bomber's turn may explain why it vanished.

38
00:02:20,985 --> 00:02:24,411
In 2015, an Energy Department
report says an unidentified

39
00:02:24,431 --> 00:02:28,219
object triggered a lockdown at a
nuclear weapons site in Texas.

40
00:02:28,459 --> 00:02:31,486
And in 2019, an aviator
with 28 years of service

41
00:02:31,506 --> 00:02:34,595
said an object moved unlike
anything he had seen.

42
00:02:35,967 --> 00:02:38,898
So what do these files prove? Not much,
yet.

43
00:02:39,138 --> 00:02:42,710
The Pentagon says some cases
stay unresolved because there

44
00:02:42,730 --> 00:02:45,931
is not enough information to
say what witnesses saw.

45
00:02:46,171 --> 00:02:50,102
None of the files described so far has
been linked to the F-22 story.

46
00:02:50,342 --> 00:02:52,758
Asked about a secret
government UFO program,

47
00:02:52,778 --> 00:02:55,249
the president said no, he
had not heard that.

48
00:02:55,489 --> 00:02:56,798
More batches are coming.

49
00:02:57,038 --> 00:03:01,984
Until then, the best evidence is still a
story with no names, no date and no data.

50
00:03:03,667 --> 00:03:07,434
Do you think these files are real
evidence, or just strange stories?

51
00:03:07,674 --> 00:03:08,594
Tell me in the comments.
